  Backups are in ~/.conveno-data/backups/2026-11-27T14-02-11.
  Restart open sessions so they pick up Conveno.
i Codex asks you to trust new hooks once: run /hooks inside Codex.
  Next: conveno status lists your sessions.
"
`;

exports[`status > groups sessions by repo and marks the orchestrator, against a real daemon 1`] = `
"daemon up · relay: off (local only) · 3 sessions

  /work/api
    SESSION       CLI  TIER       STATE  LAST SEEN
  ● claude@api-1  cl   next turn  idle   14:02:11   orchestrator
  ○ codex@api-1   cx   next turn  idle   14:02:11

  /work/docs
    SESSION          CLI  TIER   STATE  LAST SEEN
  ○ opencode@docs-1  oc   inbox  idle   14:02:11

3 sessions in 2 repos
"
`;

exports[`status > says when there are no sessions 1`] = `
"daemon up · relay: off (local only) · 0 sessions

No sessions yet. Open a supported CLI after conveno init and it appears here.
"
`;

exports[`status > warns with a fix when no daemon is running 1`] = `
"! The Conveno daemon is not running.
  why  Sessions are listed by the daemon, and nothing is listening on its socket.
  fix  Run conveno daemon start, or open a supported CLI after conveno init.
"
`;

exports[`uninstall > restores files byte for byte from the latest manifest and removes files that did not exist 1`] = `
"Conveno will undo 1 install, made 2026-11-27 14:02:11 (local time).

  ~/.claude.json           restored byte for byte
  ~/.claude/settings.json  removed, it did not exist before
  ~/.codex/config.toml     removed, it did not exist before
  ~/.codex/hooks.json      removed, it did not exist before

✓ Done. 0.0s
  Restored 4 files to how init found them.
  Restart open sessions to drop Conveno.
"
`;
